# Surface Duo: the screen does not blank and lock on its own. Closing the
# device is what puts it to sleep (the hall sensor, adaptation/system), and
# an open Duo on a desk is being looked at. The backlight still dims after
# idle (gsd-power: idle-dim, to idle-brightness percent) - with blanking off
# it dims after a fixed short delay rather than a fraction of idle-delay.
# The power button locks as before. Droidian's mobile-power-saver ties its
# hard saving (powersave governor, frozen processes) to the blanked screen,
# so with this an open device stays at full speed; idle suspend on battery
# is off in Droidian anyway (sleep-inactive-battery-type=nothing).
# A default, not a lock: a user's own value wins.
[org/gnome/desktop/session]
idle-delay=uint32 0
[org/gnome/settings-daemon/plugins/power]
idle-dim=true
idle-brightness=30
